I didn't get one response, and I'm dead!

258
00:15:04,300 --> 00:15:08,720
Well, the gay community is a lot more vocal than the dead community.

259
00:15:08,890 --> 00:15:14,770
I can't believe this. Not even my geology lab partner. And I carried that guy.

260
00:15:14,940 --> 00:15:16,900
All right. Look, let's think about this, okay?

261
00:15:17,070 --> 00:15:20,240
You think people are gonna disturb your family at this tragic time?

262
00:15:20,400 --> 00:15:23,070
That people are gonna post condolences on a website?

263
00:15:23,240 --> 00:15:25,320
This isn't about people not caring that you're dead.

264
00:15:25,490 --> 00:15:29,410
This is about people not having a decent outlet for their grief.

265
00:15:30,500 --> 00:15:33,120
You're right. There isn't a decent outlet.

266
00:15:30,500 --> 00:15:33,120
Right.

267
00:15:33,290 --> 00:15:35,670
Come on. I'm sure if you had a funeral or memorial service...

268
00:15:35,830 --> 00:15:38,090
tons of people would come.

269
00:15:38,670 --> 00:15:40,630
Exactly!

270
00:15:41,840 --> 00:15:43,430
Ross, what are you doing?

271
00:15:44,430 --> 00:15:46,680
You're having a memorial service for yourself?

272
00:15:47,140 --> 00:15:50,220
No, that would be stupid. You're having it for me.

273
00:15:51,560 --> 00:15:55,730
Ross, don't press send. Don't press...

274
00:15:51,560 --> 00:15:55,730
No, too late. Too late. It's sent.

275
00:15:55,900 --> 00:15:58,860
Sorry, so is that picture of you and the policeman.

276
00:16:01,110 --> 00:16:03,900
I'm trying to put Emma down for a nap. Have you seen Huggsy?

277
00:16:04,070 --> 00:16:05,990
Uh, original or crappy?

278
00:16:07,410 --> 00:16:09,950
Original.

279
00:16:07,410 --> 00:16:09,950
No. Sorry. Haven't seen him.

280
00:16:10,160 --> 00:16:12,870
Then what's that big lump under your covers'?

281
00:16:14,120 --> 00:16:17,500
It's Monica, okay?

282
00:16:14,120 --> 00:16:17,500
That's not Monica!

283
00:16:17,670 --> 00:16:21,000
All right, fine! It's original Huggsy!

284
00:16:22,670 --> 00:16:25,220
I know Emma wants him, but he's mine and I need him.

285
00:16:25,380 --> 00:16:28,010
She's being unreasonable.

286
00:16:28,300 --> 00:16:31,640
Joey, there is a reason that Emma loves that stupid penguin so much!

287
00:16:31,850 --> 00:16:33,930
Oh, don't cover its ears!

288
00:16:34,640 --> 00:16:38,400
It's because it reminds her of her Uncle Joey.

289
00:16:39,270 --> 00:16:40,980
It does?

290
00:16:39,270 --> 00:16:40,980
Yeah.

291
00:16:41,150 --> 00:16:46,030
And she's comforted by him because she loves her Uncle Joey so much.

292
00:16:46,240 --> 00:16:50,080
Really? She loves me?

293
00:16:46,240 --> 00:16:50,080
Oh, yeah.

294
00:16:50,280 --> 00:16:53,250
But you know what? If you need Huggsy, don't worry.

295
00:16:53,410 --> 00:16:56,620
Emma will totally understand. I won't, but whatever.

296
00:16:56,830 --> 00:17:01,380
Okay, wait a minute, wait a minute, Rach. I mean, if...

297
00:17:01,550 --> 00:17:05,170
If Huggsy means that much to Emma, then...

298
00:17:05,590 --> 00:17:06,880
Well, she can have him.

299
00:17:07,260 --> 00:17:09,970
Oh, sweet, I knew Uncle Joey would step up.

300
00:17:10,350 --> 00:17:14,140
Look, Emma. Look who's back.

301
00:17:10,350 --> 00:17:14,140
No, forget it! Forget it! I can't do it!

302
00:17:14,350 --> 00:17:17,230
Are you...? You're gonna take Huggsy away from a little child?

303
00:17:17,440 --> 00:17:19,810
How do you think I got him in the first place?

304
00:17:22,400 --> 00:17:24,740
All right, you two. I'm gonna go to the bathroom.

305
00:17:24,900 --> 00:17:26,990
I don't want anything going on while I'm gone.

306
00:17:27,240 --> 00:17:29,200
Here's a few things you can discuss:

307
00:17:29,360 --> 00:17:33,620
Mucus, fungus, and the idea of me and Ross doing it.

308
00:17:37,160 --> 00:17:38,580
I've missed you so much.

309
00:17:38,790 --> 00:17:42,630
I'm not gonna ask you to get back together. I know we want different things, but...

310
00:17:42,790 --> 00:17:45,380
Just to be with you one more night.

311
00:17:42,790 --> 00:17:45,380
I want that too.

312
00:17:45,550 --> 00:17:49,720
But is that gonna make it too hard?

313
00:17:45,550 --> 00:17:49,720
It can't be any harder than this.

314
00:17:49,930 --> 00:17:53,430
I mean, if I had known the last time I saw you would be the last time, I...

315
00:17:54,220 --> 00:17:57,230
I would have stopped to memorize your face, the way you moved.

316
00:17:57,390 --> 00:17:59,600
Everything about you.

317
00:17:59,770 --> 00:18:03,860
If I had known the last time I kissed you would be the last time...

318
00:18:04,020 --> 00:18:06,490
I never would have stopped.

319
00:18:07,780 --> 00:18:10,320
Kiss him, you fool!

320
00:18:10,990 --> 00:18:13,410
What?

321
00:18:10,990 --> 00:18:13,410
Didn't you hear that speech?

322
00:18:13,580 --> 00:18:15,830
If you don't kiss him, then I will.

323
00:18:16,580 --> 00:18:19,160
I missed you so much.

324
00:18:19,750 --> 00:18:23,380
I knew you'd be here!

325
00:18:19,750 --> 00:18:23,380
Aw, crap.

326
00:18:23,540 --> 00:18:27,380
Who is this?

327
00:18:23,540 --> 00:18:27,380
It's my friend Manny.

328
00:18:27,550 --> 00:18:30,550
I asked him to keep me away from you.

329
00:18:31,180 --> 00:18:35,560
Hey, that's what I'm doing for Phoebe.

330
00:18:31,180 --> 00:18:35,560
Well, you're not doing a very good job.

331
00:18:36,140 --> 00:18:38,270
Excuse me?

332
00:18:36,140 --> 00:18:38,270
What's with the kissing?

333
00:18:38,480 --> 00:18:41,020
Hey, at least I knew where my guy was.

334
00:18:41,190 --> 00:18:44,360
Yeah, thank God you were here to oversee all the kissing.

335
00:18:45,360 --> 00:18:48,030
You didn't hear the speech. MANNY: I've heard the speech.

336
00:18:48,240 --> 00:18:50,450
If he knew it was gonna be the last time...

337
00:18:50,610 --> 00:18:52,990
Hey, it was very moving. You're just heartless!

338
00:18:53,200 --> 00:18:55,580
You're weak!

339
00:18:53,200 --> 00:18:55,580
You're weird!

340
00:18:55,780 --> 00:18:58,410
Your pants are undone.

341
00:18:55,780 --> 00:18:58,410
Oh!

342
00:19:01,120 --> 00:19:03,250
Where'd they go?

343
00:19:04,130 --> 00:19:07,550
Damn it.

344
00:19:04,130 --> 00:19:07,550
Well, we blew it.

345
00:19:07,710 --> 00:19:09,880
I blame myself.

346
00:19:10,300 --> 00:19:12,300
And I blame you too.

347
00:19:18,720 --> 00:19:22,440
It's been an hour, and not one of my classmates has shown up?

348
00:19:22,730 --> 00:19:26,570
I tell you, when I actually die, some people are gonna get seriously haunted.

349
00:19:29,070 --> 00:19:31,030
There you go. Someone came.

350
00:19:31,240 --> 00:19:33,450
Okay. Okay. I'm gonna go hide.

351
00:19:33,610 --> 00:19:37,080
This is so exciting. My first mourner!

352
00:19:40,160 --> 00:19:42,500
Hi. Glad you could come.

353
00:19:42,660 --> 00:19:46,290
Please come in.

354
00:19:42,660 --> 00:19:46,290
Hi. You're Chandler Bing, right?

355
00:19:46,460 --> 00:19:48,790
I'm Tom Gordon. I was in your class.

356
00:19:48,790 --> 00:19:50,880
Oh, yes. Yes, let me take your coat.

357
00:19:51,050 --> 00:19:54,760
Thanks. Uh, I'm so sorry about Ross, it's...

358
00:19:54,930 --> 00:19:57,600
No, at least he died doing what he loved.

359
00:19:57,760 --> 00:20:00,060
Watching blimps.

360
00:20:05,440 --> 00:20:07,940
Who is it?

361
00:20:05,440 --> 00:20:07,940
You know some guy, Tom Gordon?

362
00:20:08,190 --> 00:20:09,570
I don't remember him.

363
00:20:09,730 --> 00:20:13,450
But then again, I touched so many lives.

364
00:20:15,740 --> 00:20:17,280
So did you know Ross well?

365
00:20:17,450 --> 00:20:20,620
Actually, I barely knew him. I came because I heard Chandler's news.

366
00:20:20,790 --> 00:20:22,700
Do you know if he's seeing anyone?

367
00:20:27,040 --> 00:20:33,420
Yes, he is. Me.

368
00:20:27,040 --> 00:20:33,420
What? You mean...? Oh.

369
00:20:34,400 --> 00:20:39,190
Can I ask you a personal question? How do you shave your beard so close'?

370
00:20:40,430 --> 00:20:42,720
Okay, Tommy! That's enough mourning for you.

371
00:20:42,890 --> 00:20:46,270
Here we go. Bye-bye. All right.

372
00:20:46,440 --> 00:20:50,230
Hey, listen. Call me.

373
00:20:46,440 --> 00:20:50,230
Okay.

374
00:20:52,530 --> 00:20:57,160
I'm dead and no one cares?

375
00:20:52,530 --> 00:20:57,160
I look like a man?

376
00:20:57,820 --> 00:21:00,740
Please, one ridiculous problem at a time.

377
00:21:00,910 --> 00:21:03,700
This isn't ridiculous. Look around, no one's here.

378
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:07,620
You gave them one day's notice. Not everyone checks the website every day.

379
00:21:07,790 --> 00:21:10,090
And Monica, it's probably the way you stand!

380
00:21:12,500 --> 00:21:15,880
I guess you're right. Still, somebody must have seen it.

381
00:21:16,050 --> 00:21:20,050
I mean, I went to that school for four years and I didn't have an impact on anyone?

382
00:21:20,220 --> 00:21:23,520
Well, that's not true. You had an impact on me.

383
00:21:23,680 --> 00:21:26,390
I mean, it's 15 years later and we're still best friends.

384
00:21:26,560 --> 00:21:28,980
Doesn't that count for something?

385
00:21:33,230 --> 00:21:36,650
Oh, great, more party boys for Chandler.

386
00:21:36,820 --> 00:21:40,570
I'm sure it's somebody for you. Now go hide.

387
00:21:44,240 --> 00:21:47,960
Hi. I'm here for Ross Geller's memorial service.

388
00:21:48,670 --> 00:21:52,340
Kori? Kori Weston?

389
00:21:48,670 --> 00:21:52,340
Yeah.

390
00:21:52,750 --> 00:21:55,510
You look amazing.

391
00:21:52,750 --> 00:21:55,510
And you are?

392
00:21:55,710 --> 00:21:59,260
Chandler. Chandler Bing. And I'm not gay. I'm not gay at all.

393
00:21:59,430 --> 00:22:01,430
You are married, though.

394
00:22:01,600 --> 00:22:04,810
Don't listen to him. He's in a really bad mood.

395
00:22:08,310 --> 00:22:11,900
I can't believe that Ross is gone. It is just so sad.

396
00:22:12,110 --> 00:22:14,150
I didn't know Ross and you were so close.

397
00:22:14,360 --> 00:22:18,200
Oh, we weren't. But we had one class together. He was such a great guy.

398
00:22:18,360 --> 00:22:21,950
And he talked so passionately about science.

399
00:22:22,120 --> 00:22:25,740
I always remembered him.

400
00:22:22,120 --> 00:22:25,740
I'm sure that would mean a lot to him.

401
00:22:25,910 --> 00:22:27,700
And if heaven has a door...

402
00:22:27,870 --> 00:22:31,670
I'm sure he's pressing his ear up against it and listening intently.

403
00:22:33,500 --> 00:22:37,510
I thought so many times about calling him and asking him out.

404
00:22:37,670 --> 00:22:39,550
I guess I really missed my chance.

405
00:22:39,970 --> 00:22:42,260
No, you didn't!

406
00:22:44,050 --> 00:22:45,850
I'm still alive!

407
00:22:47,100 --> 00:22:49,600
Kori, I know this is a big surprise for you.

408
00:22:49,810 --> 00:22:53,940
It's a long story. But the things you just said really made my day.

409
00:22:54,110 --> 00:22:56,270
The fact that you're here means more to me...

410
00:22:56,440 --> 00:22:59,150
than if this room were filled with people.

411
00:22:59,820 --> 00:23:02,320
You sick freak! Who does that?

412
00:23:02,490 --> 00:23:04,120
I can't believe I had a crush on you.

413
00:23:09,580 --> 00:23:11,370
Did you hear that?

414
00:23:11,540 --> 00:23:15,250
Kori Weston had a crush on me!

415
00:23:22,720 --> 00:23:26,140
No, Mom, I am not dead.

416
00:23:26,600 --> 00:23:29,850
I know it's not something to kid about.

417
00:23:30,560 --> 00:23:34,940
It was just a practical joke between Chandler and me, but it's over, okay?

418
00:23:35,440 --> 00:23:39,900
Actually, no. Even if I had died, you would not be left childless.

419
00:23:41,530 --> 00:23:43,360
Monica?

